  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "This would allow for creators to scale their effects properly based on the quality settings of the user. \n\nThis means that, for instance, if I'm raymarching something and I want to lower step counts for users with lower quality settings, I could do that, for performance reasons. \n\nAnother good use case would be changing the way Alpha To Coverage works based on the MSAA level. Currently, users on Desktop Low will just see a cutout-like material, rather than a nice faded transition. If we could access the Quality Settings, one could check to see what level MSAA is set to and handle it differently. \n\nAccessing the quality settings would be a pretty big quality of life improvement for shader creators.",
